A serene riverside scene in the dreamy, floating style of Marc Chagall, featuring two robed figures in saffron orange kneeling beside flowing water rendered in deep blues and purples. One figure cradles a small dark scorpion in gentle upturned palms, while ethereal golden light emanates from the gesture of compassion. The scorpion's tail curves upward but the monk's expression remains peaceful and accepting. Simple wooden bowls float nearby in the swirling current. The background dissolves into Chagall's signature fantastical elements—fish swimming through air, a crescent moon visible in daylight, scattered flowers defying gravity. The color palette blends warm earth tones with mystical blues and touches of crimson where the sting occurred, creating a meditation on kindness persisting despite inevitable pain.
